      "source": [
        "## Phase 5: Conflict Graph Construction\n",
        "\n",
        "This phase builds the weighted conflict graph from a reduced candidate-slot set.\n",
        "\n",
        "- A **node** represents one surviving `CandidateSlot`.\n",
        "- A **node weight** is the slot's computed optimization value.\n",
        "- An **edge** represents an incompatibility between two slots.\n",
        "\n",
        "The implementation uses `networkx.Graph` so later phases can reuse standard graph operations directly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "1b2eac49",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Edge Construction Rules\n",
        "\n",
        "Phase 5 implements exactly two incompatibility rules:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Same-antenna overlap conflict:** two slots on the same antenna overlap in time.\n",
        "2. **Same-antenna reconfiguration-time conflict:** two non-overlapping slots on the same antenna are closer than the required reconfiguration time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 265,
      "id": "e8f428fd",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def same_source_interval_conflict(first_slot: CandidateSlot, second_slot: CandidateSlot) -> bool:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return True when two slots are alternative placements of the same request.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return first_slot.source_interval_id == second_slot.source_interval_id\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def same_antenna_overlap_conflict(first_slot: CandidateSlot, second_slot: CandidateSlot) -> bool:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return True when two slots overlap on the same antenna.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if first_slot.antenna_id != second_slot.antenna_id:\n",
        "        return False\n",
        "\n",
        "    return intervals_overlap(\n",
        "        first_slot.start_time,\n",
        "        first_slot.end_time,\n",
        "        second_slot.start_time,\n",
        "        second_slot.end_time,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def time_gap_between_non_overlapping_slots(first_slot: CandidateSlot, second_slot: CandidateSlot) -> float:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return the time gap between two non-overlapping slots.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if first_slot.end_time <= second_slot.start_time:\n",
        "        return second_slot.start_time - first_slot.end_time\n",
        "\n",
        "    return first_slot.start_time - second_slot.end_time\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def same_antenna_reconfiguration_conflict(\n",
        "    first_slot: CandidateSlot,\n",
        "    second_slot: CandidateSlot,\n",
        ") -> bool:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return True when same-antenna slots are too close in time.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if first_slot.antenna_id != second_slot.antenna_id:\n",
        "        return False\n",
        "\n",
        "    if same_antenna_overlap_conflict(first_slot, second_slot):\n",
        "        return False\n",
        "\n",
        "    gap = time_gap_between_non_overlapping_slots(first_slot, second_slot)\n",
        "    required_gap = max(\n",
        "        first_slot.antenna.reconfiguration_time,\n",
        "        second_slot.antenna.reconfiguration_time,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return gap < required_gap\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_conflict_graph(slots: list[CandidateSlot]) -> nx.Graph:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Build a conflict graph from reduced candidate slots.\"\"\"\n",
        "    graph = nx.Graph()\n",
        "\n",
        "    for slot in slots:\n",
        "        graph.add_node(\n",
        "            slot.slot_id,\n",
        "            slot=slot,\n",
        "            weight=slot.weight,\n",
        "            source_interval_id=slot.source_interval_id,\n",
        "            satellite_id=slot.satellite_id,\n",
        "            antenna_id=slot.antenna_id,\n",
        "            station_id=slot.station_id,\n",
        "            reconfiguration_time=slot.antenna.reconfiguration_time,\n",
        "            start_time=slot.start_time,\n",
        "            end_time=slot.end_time,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    for first_slot, second_slot in combinations(slots, 2):\n",
        "        if same_source_interval_conflict(first_slot, second_slot):\n",
        "            graph.add_edge(\n",
        "                first_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                second_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                reason=\"same communication request\",\n",
        "                source_interval_id=first_slot.source_interval_id,\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        elif same_antenna_overlap_conflict(first_slot, second_slot):\n",
        "            graph.add_edge(first_slot.slot_id, second_slot.slot_id, reason=\"same-antenna overlap\")\n",
        "        elif same_antenna_reconfiguration_conflict(first_slot, second_slot):\n",
        "            graph.add_edge(\n",
        "                first_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                second_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                reason=\"same-antenna reconfiguration time\",\n",
        "                reconfiguration_time=max(\n",
        "                    first_slot.antenna.reconfiguration_time,\n",
        "                    second_slot.antenna.reconfiguration_time,\n",
        "                ),\n",
        "            )\n",
        "\n",
        "    return graph\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5f616784",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Graph Diagnostics\n",
        "\n",
        "The diagnostics summarize the graph size and structure. Connected components are computed here only as a diagnostic; later phases may use components more directly for QPU subproblem selection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 266,
      "id": "4b7ca69a",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def connected_components(graph: nx.Graph) -> list[set[str]]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return connected components of the conflict graph.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return [set(component) for component in nx.connected_components(graph)]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def graph_diagnostics(graph: nx.Graph) -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Compute basic diagnostics for a conflict graph.\"\"\"\n",
        "    node_count = graph.number_of_nodes()\n",
        "    edge_count = graph.number_of_edges()\n",
        "    average_degree = 0.0 if node_count == 0 else sum(dict(graph.degree()).values()) / node_count\n",
        "    density = nx.density(graph)\n",
        "    components = connected_components(graph)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"node_count\": node_count,\n",
        "        \"edge_count\": edge_count,\n",
        "        \"average_degree\": average_degree,\n",
        "        \"density\": density,\n",
        "        \"connected_components\": components,\n",
        "        \"component_count\": len(components),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def print_conflict_graph(graph: nx.Graph) -> None:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Print nodes, edges, and diagnostics for readable notebook inspection.\"\"\"\n",
        "    diagnostics = graph_diagnostics(graph)\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"Nodes:\")\n",
        "    for slot_id in sorted(graph.nodes):\n",
        "        slot = graph.nodes[slot_id][\"slot\"]\n",
        "        print({\"slot_id\": slot_id, \"source_interval_id\": slot.source_interval_id, \"antenna_id\": slot.antenna_id, \"start_time\": slot.start_time, \"end_time\": slot.end_time, \"weight\": slot.weight})\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\nEdges:\")\n",
        "    for first_slot_id, second_slot_id, edge_data in sorted(graph.edges(data=True)):\n",
        "        edge_summary = {\"edge\": (first_slot_id, second_slot_id), \"reason\": edge_data[\"reason\"]}\n",
        "        if \"source_interval_id\" in edge_data:\n",
        "            edge_summary[\"source_interval_id\"] = edge_data[\"source_interval_id\"]\n",
        "        print(edge_summary)\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\nDiagnostics:\")\n",
        "    print({\"node_count\": diagnostics[\"node_count\"], \"edge_count\": diagnostics[\"edge_count\"]})\n",
        "    print({\"average_degree\": diagnostics[\"average_degree\"], \"density\": diagnostics[\"density\"]})\n",
        "    print({\"component_count\": diagnostics[\"component_count\"], \"connected_components\": diagnostics[\"connected_components\"]})\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "63bae0f9",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Phase 5 Shared Dataset Conflict Graph\n",
        "\n",
        "The conflict graph is built from the Phase 4 candidate set. Nodes are surviving candidate slots, and edges are same-antenna timing conflicts.\n"
      ]
    },
