      "source": [
        "## Phase 6: MWIS Validation and Classical Reference\n",
        "\n",
        "This phase validates the maximum-weight independent set abstraction and computes a classical reference solution for the conflict graph. The QUBO translation comes in Phase 7.\n",
        "\n",
        "In the conflict graph:\n",
        "- selecting a node means selecting the corresponding candidate slot,\n",
        "- node weights are slot values,\n",
        "- and conflict edges enforce that incompatible slots cannot both be selected.\n",
        "\n",
        "Therefore, a feasible schedule corresponds to an independent set, and the best schedule under this simplified model corresponds to a maximum-weight independent set.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "9357e9c6",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Classical MWIS Reference Solver\n",
        "\n",
        "MWIS is NP-hard, so Phase 6 now uses a two-level strategy.\n",
        "\n",
        "First, it decomposes the conflict graph into connected components. This is exact because disconnected components do not constrain each other.\n",
        "\n",
        "Second, it solves each component according to size:\n",
        "- small components are solved exactly,\n",
        "- bounded medium components use the exact complement-clique transformation,\n",
        "- larger components fall back to a deterministic weighted greedy heuristic.\n",
        "\n",
        "The large-component fallback keeps the pipeline moving on dense or difficult datasets. When it is used, the result is marked as `heuristic_feasible` instead of `optimal`, so downstream phases know whether the Phase 6 result is an exact reference or a feasible classical baseline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 270,
      "id": "ad0910a0",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "MAX_EXACT_MWIS_COMPONENT_NODES = 35\n",
        "EXACT_ENUMERATION_COMPONENT_LIMIT = 22\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def is_independent_node_set(graph: nx.Graph, selected_node_ids: set[str]) -> bool:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return True when no selected node pair is connected by a conflict edge.\"\"\"\n",
        "    for first_node, second_node in combinations(selected_node_ids, 2):\n",
        "        if graph.has_edge(first_node, second_node):\n",
        "            return False\n",
        "\n",
        "    return True\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_node_set_weight(graph: nx.Graph, selected_node_ids: set[str]) -> float:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Compute the total graph weight of selected nodes.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return sum(graph.nodes[node_id][\"weight\"] for node_id in selected_node_ids)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def solve_mwis_by_enumeration(graph: nx.Graph) -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Solve MWIS exactly by enumerating all node subsets.\n",
        "\n",
        "    This fallback is exponential and intended only for small connected\n",
        "    components, not for the full realistic graph.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    node_ids = sorted(graph.nodes)\n",
        "    best_selected_node_ids = set()\n",
        "    best_objective_value = 0.0\n",
        "\n",
        "    for subset_size in range(len(node_ids) + 1):\n",
        "        for node_subset in combinations(node_ids, subset_size):\n",
        "            selected_node_ids = set(node_subset)\n",
        "\n",
        "            if not is_independent_node_set(graph, selected_node_ids):\n",
        "                continue\n",
        "\n",
        "            objective_value = compute_node_set_weight(graph, selected_node_ids)\n",
        "            if objective_value > best_objective_value:\n",
        "                best_selected_node_ids = selected_node_ids\n",
        "                best_objective_value = objective_value\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"selected_node_ids\": best_selected_node_ids,\n",
        "        \"objective_value\": best_objective_value,\n",
        "        \"solver\": \"exact enumeration\",\n",
        "        \"status\": \"optimal\",\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def solve_mwis_with_networkx_clique(\n",
        "    graph: nx.Graph,\n",
        "    weight_scale: int = 1000,\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Solve MWIS exactly as maximum-weight clique on the complement graph.\n",
        "\n",
        "    NetworkX 2.8 expects integer clique weights, so float slot weights are\n",
        "    scaled for the solver while the returned objective uses the original\n",
        "    graph weights. This is used only for bounded connected components.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    complement_graph = nx.complement(graph)\n",
        "\n",
        "    for node_id, node_data in graph.nodes(data=True):\n",
        "        complement_graph.nodes[node_id][\"scaled_weight\"] = int(\n",
        "            round(node_data[\"weight\"] * weight_scale)\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    selected_node_ids, scaled_objective_value = nx.algorithms.clique.max_weight_clique(\n",
        "        complement_graph,\n",
        "        weight=\"scaled_weight\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    selected_node_ids = set(selected_node_ids)\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"selected_node_ids\": selected_node_ids,\n",
        "        \"objective_value\": compute_node_set_weight(graph, selected_node_ids),\n",
        "        \"solver\": \"NetworkX exact max-weight clique on component complement\",\n",
        "        \"status\": \"optimal\",\n",
        "        \"weight_scale\": weight_scale,\n",
        "        \"reported_scaled_clique_weight\": scaled_objective_value,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def solve_mwis_by_weighted_greedy(graph: nx.Graph) -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Build a feasible weighted independent set for a large component.\n",
        "\n",
        "    This is a deterministic heuristic, not an exact MWIS solver. Nodes are\n",
        "    ranked by weight divided by local conflict pressure, then greedily selected\n",
        "    while removing neighbors.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    remaining_node_ids = set(graph.nodes)\n",
        "    selected_node_ids = set()\n",
        "\n",
        "    while remaining_node_ids:\n",
        "        best_node_id = max(\n",
        "            remaining_node_ids,\n",
        "            key=lambda node_id: (\n",
        "                graph.nodes[node_id][\"weight\"] / (1 + graph.degree(node_id)),\n",
        "                graph.nodes[node_id][\"weight\"],\n",
        "                -graph.degree(node_id),\n",
        "                node_id,\n",
        "            ),\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        selected_node_ids.add(best_node_id)\n",
        "        remaining_node_ids.remove(best_node_id)\n",
        "        remaining_node_ids.difference_update(graph.neighbors(best_node_id))\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"selected_node_ids\": selected_node_ids,\n",
        "        \"objective_value\": compute_node_set_weight(graph, selected_node_ids),\n",
        "        \"solver\": \"deterministic weighted greedy independent-set heuristic\",\n",
        "        \"status\": \"heuristic_feasible\",\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def solve_connected_component_mwis(graph: nx.Graph) -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Solve MWIS exactly on one connected component with size guards.\"\"\"\n",
        "    node_count = graph.number_of_nodes()\n",
        "    if node_count == 0:\n",
        "        return {\n",
        "            \"selected_node_ids\": set(),\n",
        "            \"objective_value\": 0.0,\n",
        "            \"solver\": \"empty component\",\n",
        "            \"status\": \"optimal\",\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    if node_count == 1:\n",
        "        node_id = next(iter(graph.nodes))\n",
        "        return {\n",
        "            \"selected_node_ids\": {node_id},\n",
        "            \"objective_value\": compute_node_set_weight(graph, {node_id}),\n",
        "            \"solver\": \"single-node component shortcut\",\n",
        "            \"status\": \"optimal\",\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    if node_count > MAX_EXACT_MWIS_COMPONENT_NODES:\n",
        "        return solve_mwis_by_weighted_greedy(graph)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if node_count <= EXACT_ENUMERATION_COMPONENT_LIMIT:\n",
        "        return solve_mwis_by_enumeration(graph)\n",
        "    return solve_mwis_with_networkx_clique(graph)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def solve_mwis_by_connected_components(graph: nx.Graph) -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Solve MWIS exactly by decomposing the conflict graph into components.\"\"\"\n",
        "    selected_node_ids = set()\n",
        "    component_results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    components = sorted(\n",
        "        nx.connected_components(graph),\n",
        "        key=lambda component: (-len(component), sorted(component)),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    for component_index, component_node_ids in enumerate(components, start=1):\n",
        "        component_graph = graph.subgraph(component_node_ids).copy()\n",
        "        component_result = solve_connected_component_mwis(component_graph)\n",
        "        selected_node_ids.update(component_result[\"selected_node_ids\"])\n",
        "        component_results.append(\n",
        "            {\n",
        "                \"component_index\": component_index,\n",
        "                \"node_count\": component_graph.number_of_nodes(),\n",
        "                \"edge_count\": component_graph.number_of_edges(),\n",
        "                \"selected_node_count\": len(component_result[\"selected_node_ids\"]),\n",
        "                \"objective_value\": component_result[\"objective_value\"],\n",
        "                \"solver\": component_result[\"solver\"],\n",
        "                \"status\": component_result[\"status\"],\n",
        "            }\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    overall_status = (\n",
        "        \"optimal\"\n",
        "        if all(component_result[\"status\"] == \"optimal\" for component_result in component_results)\n",
        "        else \"heuristic_feasible\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"selected_node_ids\": selected_node_ids,\n",
        "        \"objective_value\": compute_node_set_weight(graph, selected_node_ids),\n",
        "        \"solver\": \"MWIS by connected components with large-component heuristic fallback\",\n",
        "        \"status\": overall_status,\n",
        "        \"component_count\": len(components),\n",
        "        \"max_component_size\": max((len(component) for component in components), default=0),\n",
        "        \"heuristic_component_count\": sum(\n",
        "            1 for component_result in component_results\n",
        "            if component_result[\"status\"] != \"optimal\"\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        \"component_results\": component_results,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def solve_mwis_classically(graph: nx.Graph) -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Compute a classical reference MWIS solution without global clique blow-up.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return solve_mwis_by_connected_components(graph)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5bc9d878",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Schedule Reconstruction and Feasibility Check\n",
        "\n",
        "After solving MWIS, the selected graph nodes are mapped back to `CandidateSlot` objects. The reconstructed schedule is then checked directly against the simplified Phase 5 conflict rules."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 271,
      "id": "e69439ad",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def reconstruct_selected_schedule(graph: nx.Graph, selected_node_ids: set[str]) -> list[CandidateSlot]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Map selected graph node ids back to candidate slots.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return [graph.nodes[node_id][\"slot\"] for node_id in sorted(selected_node_ids)]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def check_schedule_feasibility(\n",
        "    selected_slots: list[CandidateSlot],\n",
        ") -> tuple[bool, list[Dict[str, str]]]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Check selected slots against overlap and antenna-specific reconfiguration conflicts.\"\"\"\n",
        "    conflicts = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for first_slot, second_slot in combinations(selected_slots, 2):\n",
        "        if same_source_interval_conflict(first_slot, second_slot):\n",
        "            conflicts.append(\n",
        "                {\n",
        "                    \"first_slot_id\": first_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                    \"second_slot_id\": second_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                    \"reason\": \"same communication request\",\n",
        "                }\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        elif same_antenna_overlap_conflict(first_slot, second_slot):\n",
        "            conflicts.append(\n",
        "                {\n",
        "                    \"first_slot_id\": first_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                    \"second_slot_id\": second_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                    \"reason\": \"same-antenna overlap\",\n",
        "                }\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        elif same_antenna_reconfiguration_conflict(first_slot, second_slot):\n",
        "            conflicts.append(\n",
        "                {\n",
        "                    \"first_slot_id\": first_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                    \"second_slot_id\": second_slot.slot_id,\n",
        "                    \"reason\": \"same-antenna reconfiguration time\",\n",
        "                }\n",
        "            )\n",
        "\n",
        "    return len(conflicts) == 0, conflicts\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def validate_mwis_solution(\n",
        "    graph: nx.Graph,\n",
        "    selected_node_ids: set[str],\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Validate the MWIS solution against graph and schedule constraints.\"\"\"\n",
        "    selected_slots = reconstruct_selected_schedule(graph, selected_node_ids)\n",
        "    schedule_is_feasible, schedule_conflicts = check_schedule_feasibility(selected_slots)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"is_independent_set\": is_independent_node_set(graph, selected_node_ids),\n",
        "        \"schedule_is_feasible\": schedule_is_feasible,\n",
        "        \"schedule_conflicts\": schedule_conflicts,\n",
        "        \"objective_value\": compute_node_set_weight(graph, selected_node_ids),\n",
        "        \"selected_slot_count\": len(selected_node_ids),\n",
        "    }\n"
      ]
    },
