      "source": [
        "## Phase 7: QUBO Construction\n",
        "\n",
        "This phase translates the MWIS conflict graph into QUBO form. We are not sampling or solving the QUBO yet; that comes after we choose QPU-sized subproblems.\n",
        "\n",
        "For one binary variable `x_i` per graph node:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `x_i = 1` means candidate slot `i` is selected,\n",
        "- the linear term `-weight_i * x_i` rewards selecting valuable nodes,\n",
        "- the quadratic term `penalty * x_i * x_j` punishes selecting both endpoints of a conflict edge.\n",
        "\n",
        "The minimization energy is:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "E(x) = -sum(weight_i * x_i) + penalty * sum(x_i * x_j for every conflict edge)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "For any conflict-free independent set, the penalty term is zero and the QUBO energy is simply the negative schedule objective.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "6f25853e",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUBO Builder\n",
        "\n",
        "The QUBO is represented as a dictionary keyed by variable pairs:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `(node_id, node_id)` stores a linear coefficient,\n",
        "- `(first_node_id, second_node_id)` stores a quadratic conflict coefficient.\n",
        "\n",
        "Because QUBO solvers minimize energy, node weights become negative diagonal coefficients. Conflict edges become positive quadratic penalties.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 275,
      "id": "7e2ca22b",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "Qubo = Dict[tuple[str, str], float]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def default_mwis_penalty(graph: nx.Graph, margin: float = 1.0) -> float:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Choose a simple penalty that dominates any single node reward.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if graph.number_of_nodes() == 0:\n",
        "        return margin\n",
        "\n",
        "    max_weight = max(graph.nodes[node_id][\"weight\"] for node_id in graph.nodes)\n",
        "    return max_weight + margin\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def canonical_qubo_key(first_node: str, second_node: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return a stable QUBO key for a linear or quadratic coefficient.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if first_node == second_node:\n",
        "        return (first_node, second_node)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return tuple(sorted((first_node, second_node)))\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_mwis_qubo(\n",
        "    graph: nx.Graph,\n",
        "    penalty: float | None = None,\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Build a minimization QUBO for the MWIS conflict graph.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if penalty is None:\n",
        "        penalty = default_mwis_penalty(graph)\n",
        "\n",
        "    qubo: Qubo = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "    for node_id, node_data in graph.nodes(data=True):\n",
        "        qubo[(node_id, node_id)] = -float(node_data[\"weight\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "    for first_node, second_node in graph.edges:\n",
        "        key = canonical_qubo_key(first_node, second_node)\n",
        "        qubo[key] = qubo.get(key, 0.0) + float(penalty)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"qubo\": qubo,\n",
        "        \"variables\": sorted(graph.nodes),\n",
        "        \"penalty\": penalty,\n",
        "        \"offset\": 0.0,\n",
        "    }\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cfae1484",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUBO Diagnostics and Energy Evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "These helper functions make the QUBO readable and testable before any quantum or heuristic sampler is introduced.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 276,
      "id": "6f3f171e",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def selected_nodes_to_binary_sample(\n",
        "    variables: list[str],\n",
        "    selected_node_ids: set[str],\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, int]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Convert a set of selected graph nodes into a binary sample dictionary.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        variable: 1 if variable in selected_node_ids else 0\n",
        "        for variable in variables\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def evaluate_qubo_energy(qubo_model: Dict[str, object], sample: Dict[str, int]) -> float:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Evaluate QUBO energy for a binary sample.\"\"\"\n",
        "    energy = float(qubo_model[\"offset\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "    for (first_node, second_node), coefficient in qubo_model[\"qubo\"].items():\n",
        "        energy += coefficient * sample[first_node] * sample[second_node]\n",
        "\n",
        "    return energy\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def qubo_diagnostics(qubo_model: Dict[str, object]) -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Report compact diagnostics for a QUBO model.\"\"\"\n",
        "    qubo = qubo_model[\"qubo\"]\n",
        "    linear_coefficients = [\n",
        "        coefficient\n",
        "        for (first_node, second_node), coefficient in qubo.items()\n",
        "        if first_node == second_node\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    quadratic_coefficients = [\n",
        "        coefficient\n",
        "        for (first_node, second_node), coefficient in qubo.items()\n",
        "        if first_node != second_node\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    all_coefficients = linear_coefficients + quadratic_coefficients\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"num_variables\": len(qubo_model[\"variables\"]),\n",
        "        \"num_linear_terms\": len(linear_coefficients),\n",
        "        \"num_quadratic_couplings\": len(quadratic_coefficients),\n",
        "        \"penalty\": qubo_model[\"penalty\"],\n",
        "        \"linear_coefficient_range\": (\n",
        "            min(linear_coefficients),\n",
        "            max(linear_coefficients),\n",
        "        ) if linear_coefficients else None,\n",
        "        \"quadratic_coefficient_range\": (\n",
        "            min(quadratic_coefficients),\n",
        "            max(quadratic_coefficients),\n",
        "        ) if quadratic_coefficients else None,\n",
        "        \"coefficient_range\": (\n",
        "            min(all_coefficients),\n",
        "            max(all_coefficients),\n",
        "        ) if all_coefficients else None,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def format_qubo_terms(\n",
        "    qubo_model: Dict[str, object],\n",
        "    max_terms: int = 20,\n",
        ") -> list[dict[str, object]]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return readable QUBO terms for notebook display.\"\"\"\n",
        "    formatted_terms = []\n",
        "    for (first_node, second_node), coefficient in sorted(qubo_model[\"qubo\"].items()):\n",
        "        formatted_terms.append(\n",
        "            {\n",
        "                \"term\": (first_node, second_node),\n",
        "                \"type\": \"linear\" if first_node == second_node else \"quadratic\",\n",
        "                \"coefficient\": coefficient,\n",
        "            }\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    return formatted_terms[:max_terms]\n"
      ]
    },
