      "source": [
        "## Phase 9: Simulated Annealing Execution Wrapper\n",
        "\n",
        "Phase 9 executes one QPU-suitable QUBO subproblem from Phase 8 using a simulated annealing backend. This is not real quantum hardware yet. It is a local annealing-style sampler that uses the same QUBO input shape we will later pass to hardware-oriented tooling.\n",
        "\n",
        "This stage introduces the execution interface that later hardware runs will need: repeated sampling, decoding binary samples back into selected candidate slots, feasibility checks against the conflict graph, objective evaluation, and comparison against the exact classical MWIS baseline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "11a29d9b",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Annealing Backend Import\n",
        "\n",
        "The current backend is D-Wave Ocean's `neal.SimulatedAnnealingSampler`. It samples low-energy binary assignments for a QUBO. A lower QUBO energy should correspond to a better schedule, provided conflict penalties are large enough and the returned sample is feasible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 284,
      "id": "bae55589",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import neal\n",
        "\n",
        "ANNEALING_BACKEND_NAME = \"neal simulated annealing\"\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "31d5c1eb",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Decoding and Evaluation Helpers\n",
        "\n",
        "The sampler returns a binary sample such as `{SLOT_000001: 1, SLOT_000002: 0}`. The helpers below decode that into selected graph nodes, evaluate the QUBO energy, check graph feasibility, and compare the sampled result with the exact MWIS solution on the same subproblem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 285,
      "id": "58dd69bd",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def sample_to_selected_node_ids(sample: Dict[str, int]) -> set[str]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Decode a binary QUBO sample into selected graph node ids.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        node_id\n",
        "        for node_id, value in sample.items()\n",
        "        if int(value) == 1\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def selected_conflict_edges(\n",
        "    graph: nx.Graph,\n",
        "    selected_node_ids: set[str],\n",
        ") -> list[tuple[str, str, str]]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return conflict edges whose endpoints are both selected.\"\"\"\n",
        "    conflicts = []\n",
        "    for first_node, second_node, edge_data in graph.edges(data=True):\n",
        "        if first_node in selected_node_ids and second_node in selected_node_ids:\n",
        "            conflicts.append((first_node, second_node, edge_data.get(\"reason\", \"unknown\")))\n",
        "\n",
        "    return conflicts\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def evaluate_annealing_sample(\n",
        "    subproblem: Dict[str, object],\n",
        "    sample: Dict[str, int],\n",
        "    energy: float,\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Evaluate one annealer sample against the graph and QUBO model.\"\"\"\n",
        "    graph = subproblem[\"graph\"]\n",
        "    qubo_model = subproblem[\"qubo\"]\n",
        "    selected_node_ids = sample_to_selected_node_ids(sample)\n",
        "    conflict_edges = selected_conflict_edges(graph, selected_node_ids)\n",
        "    objective_value = compute_node_set_weight(graph, selected_node_ids)\n",
        "    recomputed_energy = evaluate_qubo_energy(qubo_model, sample)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"selected_node_ids\": selected_node_ids,\n",
        "        \"selected_node_count\": len(selected_node_ids),\n",
        "        \"objective_value\": objective_value,\n",
        "        \"energy\": float(energy),\n",
        "        \"recomputed_energy\": recomputed_energy,\n",
        "        \"is_independent_set\": len(conflict_edges) == 0,\n",
        "        \"conflict_count\": len(conflict_edges),\n",
        "        \"conflict_edges\": conflict_edges,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def compare_sample_to_exact_mwis(\n",
        "    subproblem: Dict[str, object],\n",
        "    sample_evaluation: Dict[str, object],\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Compare annealer output against exact MWIS on the same component.\"\"\"\n",
        "    exact_solution = solve_mwis_classically(subproblem[\"graph\"])\n",
        "    exact_selected_node_ids = exact_solution[\"selected_node_ids\"]\n",
        "    exact_objective = exact_solution[\"objective_value\"]\n",
        "    sampled_objective = sample_evaluation[\"objective_value\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"exact_selected_node_ids\": exact_selected_node_ids,\n",
        "        \"exact_objective_value\": exact_objective,\n",
        "        \"sampled_objective_value\": sampled_objective,\n",
        "        \"objective_gap\": exact_objective - sampled_objective,\n",
        "        \"matches_exact_selected_set\": sample_evaluation[\"selected_node_ids\"] == exact_selected_node_ids,\n",
        "        \"matches_exact_objective\": math.isclose(\n",
        "            sampled_objective,\n",
        "            exact_objective,\n",
        "            rel_tol=1e-9,\n",
        "            abs_tol=1e-9,\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        \"exact_solver\": exact_solution[\"solver\"],\n",
        "    }\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "abbae26f",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Simulated Annealing Wrapper\n",
        "\n",
        "The wrapper accepts a Phase 8 subproblem and returns one consistent result dictionary. Later, this is the function shape we can reuse for a real quantum annealing backend: the inside changes, while the rest of the notebook can keep using the same output fields."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 286,
      "id": "3f256811",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def run_neal_simulated_annealing(\n",
        "    subproblem: Dict[str, object],\n",
        "    num_reads: int = 200,\n",
        "    seed: int | None = 42,\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Run D-Wave Neal's simulated annealer on one QUBO subproblem.\"\"\"\n",
        "    sampler = neal.SimulatedAnnealingSampler()\n",
        "    response = sampler.sample_qubo(\n",
        "        subproblem[\"qubo\"][\"qubo\"],\n",
        "        num_reads=num_reads,\n",
        "        seed=seed,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    best_record = response.first\n",
        "    best_sample = {\n",
        "        variable: int(best_record.sample[variable])\n",
        "        for variable in subproblem[\"qubo\"][\"variables\"]\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    sample_evaluation = evaluate_annealing_sample(\n",
        "        subproblem,\n",
        "        best_sample,\n",
        "        best_record.energy,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    exact_comparison = compare_sample_to_exact_mwis(\n",
        "        subproblem,\n",
        "        sample_evaluation,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"backend\": ANNEALING_BACKEND_NAME,\n",
        "        \"component_id\": subproblem[\"component_id\"],\n",
        "        \"num_reads\": num_reads,\n",
        "        \"seed\": seed,\n",
        "        \"best_sample\": best_sample,\n",
        "        \"best_energy\": float(best_record.energy),\n",
        "        \"num_occurrences\": int(best_record.num_occurrences),\n",
        "        \"sample_evaluation\": sample_evaluation,\n",
        "        \"exact_comparison\": exact_comparison,\n",
        "        \"response_info\": dict(response.info),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def run_annealing_subproblem(\n",
        "    subproblem: Dict[str, object],\n",
        "    backend: str = \"neal\",\n",
        "    num_reads: int = 200,\n",
        "    seed: int | None = 42,\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, object]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Run an annealing backend on a selected Phase 8 subproblem.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if backend != \"neal\":\n",
        "        raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported backend: {backend}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    return run_neal_simulated_annealing(\n",
        "        subproblem,\n",
        "        num_reads=num_reads,\n",
        "        seed=seed,\n",
        "    )\n"
      ]
    },
    {
